Subject: [PATCH 04/18] =?UTF-8?q?r9q:=20quitar=20interfaces=20HIDL=20de=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?Samsung=20de=20los=20rc=20de=20NFC=20y=20c=C3=A1mara?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

host_init_verifier las rechaza porque no hay hidl_interface para ellas.
Change-Id: I6adf940bbd0eee9fd0852e37a07ebc9384d45b5b
---
 extract-files.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/extract-files.py b/extract-files.py
index d11191b..c5ddc56 100755
--- a/extract-files.py
+++ b/extract-files.py
@@ -23,6 +23,13 @@ namespace_imports = [
 
 
 blob_fixups: blob_fixups_user_type = {
+    # Interfaces HIDL de Samsung sin hidl_interface en el build: host_init_verifier
+    # las rechaza. Los servicios se registran igual al arrancar con class hal
+    (
+        'vendor/etc/init/nxp.android.hardware.nfc@1.2-service.rc',
+        'vendor/etc/init/vendor.samsung.hardware.camera.provider@4.0-service_64.rc',
+    ): blob_fixup()
+        .regex_replace(r'\n[ \t]*interface vendor\.samsung\.hardware\.[^\n]*', ''),
     'vendor/lib64/hw/camera.qcom.so': blob_fixup()
         .binary_regex_replace(b'ro.boot.flash.locked', b'ro.camera.notify_nfc'),
     'vendor/lib64/hw/com.qti.chi.override.so': blob_fixup()
